[{:db/id "q-275781/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "93332e7a-22dc-586a-aa99-51e6084817fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275781/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b9a1ffe-e77f-5ccb-9605-6219c28cdf38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275781/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-275781/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275781/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "16829971-5742-5fdd-be3c-ba81e527b5db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275781/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "631d66aa-0440-5de3-bc37-8981c7fb0a9c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275781/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-275781/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275781/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "29e64051-2d06-5f61-9634-020fe9ceaeaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275781/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "33bb1b68-7b77-5cb0-940f-c98a7d0ea2a2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275781/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-275781/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275781" :question/id #uuid "15fa7367-7a5a-51c5-9948-2a491219ff01" :question/math-academy-id "q-275781" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z=-1 \\\\ x-y+3z=2 \\\\ -2x+y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, and the inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe solution of the system of equations is \n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}, \n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}, \n$\\,z=$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is \n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=0,\\,z=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275781/field-1" "q-275781/field-2" "q-275781/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78549/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "3e23a988-7da9-5ad5-95f8-147019a91511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78549/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6c66bf0b-6be0-5943-b111-5c84e064aa35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78549/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d09d984d-3d3e-56e7-9202-f43ed7b66b83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78549/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d8e1fe7d-634b-54fe-a5bb-6a19739fea21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78549/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "989434c1-5d99-5227-b61f-32a54e245304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78549/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f82a1774-d3df-54eb-a09c-156f28f43d92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78549/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-78549/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-78549/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-78549/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-78549/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-78549/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78549" :question/id #uuid "c98c808b-049b-59b0-8d36-61df2339933c" :question/math-academy-id "q-78549" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+4z=-2 \\\\ x+3y+9z=0 \\\\ y+6z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=-3,z=1.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+(-3)+1=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78549/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78549"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78550/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "1568d905-18fa-50b5-9562-361d3b23b9d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78550/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "850bffd3-2739-5528-a6b4-f2c43c0021f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78550/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "9a033ce1-2eab-56d0-8e2d-f0cd942aec7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78550/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "501aa2bb-f083-55a6-a2ab-f37d4401b4c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78550/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1b50640b-8aa5-58cd-bbe7-92f37182ac8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78550/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd296e1-f09c-5aaf-a8d7-a79b92618f6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78550/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-78550/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-78550/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-78550/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-78550/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-78550/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78550" :question/id #uuid "9be1f1c0-fd23-5eb4-a0b2-c49ac6ad11b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-78550" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-2z=-2 \\\\ 5x+y+z=-1 \\\\ -8x+2y+z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -13 & -15 & -11 \\\\ 18 & 22 & 16\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -13 & -15 & -11 \\\\ 18 & 22 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=4,z=-5.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+4+(-5)=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78550/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78550"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78552/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e55afcce-2996-5635-b9ea-176b23818cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78552/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "faef8a14-8b5c-5c54-a043-ad60bd81250b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78552/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c7695934-27b5-5fcc-8272-7671191ba8f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78552/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "84e56211-bde0-55e8-a309-ef08c3fc55d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78552/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "43e027d9-be15-5a72-b1eb-d85902b998c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78552/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8799bf71-7fdd-51d1-ab92-7506c948cc63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78552/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-78552/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-78552/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-78552/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-78552/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-78552/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78552" :question/id #uuid "07f12953-92a4-55d6-afcb-39fb0f43a712" :question/math-academy-id "q-78552" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z=-4 \\\\ -4x+4y-3z=7 \\\\ x-y+z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=2,z=-1.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+2+(-1)=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78552/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78552"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-78557"] :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z=2 \\\\ x-2y-5z=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y+2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=5,y=3,z=0.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=5+3+0=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-104546/selection/f869f8717f62845f086db3db361502d749e771dd30fc6e0a242514dacf382d6d" :answer/id #uuid "9c0dcabf-147c-5337-b739-a1164de7663f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1,y=-2,z=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104546/selection/a7bac10d7d38265aaea0bc6bdf894ae3f70492108d2081b364fba03d1373715b" :answer/id #uuid "5f9aa285-b347-55f7-b50c-db4256a8ebef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2,y=1,z=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104546/selection/12a6627518fdf73d2d2575cae242216cfbf93c5b839e111315cc55cc9fd66c19" :answer/id #uuid "97f7b19f-7238-574d-9b40-4fbe8a044044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,y=-1,z=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104546/selection/cb8d10afe1b16f6882f1a7ab326f10ea0b539eadd98dcbeb06ed0e1fba66512b" :answer/id #uuid "d4e0e71f-53b3-577f-81d7-8f5ff184d353" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1,y=1,z=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104546/selection/de4eb5785d6679bedd82b2954b12a2e8f19dd88496ef935134b271d725d274fe" :answer/id #uuid "5e5d035f-373a-5cca-9fba-bba05fe58417" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1,y=2,z=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104546/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e25e9f-66fd-5ed7-8dec-a573a810c413" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104546/selection/de4eb5785d6679bedd82b2954b12a2e8f19dd88496ef935134b271d725d274fe" :answer-field/choices ["q-104546/selection/f869f8717f62845f086db3db361502d749e771dd30fc6e0a242514dacf382d6d" "q-104546/selection/a7bac10d7d38265aaea0bc6bdf894ae3f70492108d2081b364fba03d1373715b" "q-104546/selection/12a6627518fdf73d2d2575cae242216cfbf93c5b839e111315cc55cc9fd66c19" "q-104546/selection/cb8d10afe1b16f6882f1a7ab326f10ea0b539eadd98dcbeb06ed0e1fba66512b" "q-104546/selection/de4eb5785d6679bedd82b2954b12a2e8f19dd88496ef935134b271d725d274fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104546" :question/id #uuid "3ecbb0e1-b9dd-5dc5-b4fe-5729eb70c965" :question/math-academy-id "q-104546" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}z+x=2 \\\\ 2y-3z=1 \\\\ 2z-y=-3x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+z=2 \\\\ 2y-3z=1 \\\\ 3x-y+2z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4-3)-0+(0-6) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -9 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=1,y=2,z=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104546/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104546"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42449"] :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3+z=0 \\\\ 5y-1+3x=2z+1 \\\\ 3z+2x-1=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+z=3 \\\\ 3x+5y-2z=2 \\\\ 2x-2y+3z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(15-4)+(-6-10) \\\\  & =22-16 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & 13 & -16 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -13 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=4-4-5=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-9722"] :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z+x=-1 \\\\ 4z+y=1 \\\\ 5x+6y-3=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=-1 \\\\ y+4z=1 \\\\ 5x+6y=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-24)-2(-20)+3(-5) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & -20 & -5 \\\\ -18 & -15 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 20 & -5 \\\\ 18 & -15 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}42 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=42,y=-35,z=9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-275787/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "bc761467-a3f5-54a8-83fe-e813e7574317" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275787/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "716d1d1a-decc-5153-a5ca-c4bb3512cafb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275787/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "67debf65-e6b8-50eb-a982-2a4084d044d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275787/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-275787/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-275787/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275787/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "5d432c89-df76-51ba-adc2-3657d2b6b737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275787/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "39d6b377-ea9f-5025-a00c-bcac1c32bf93" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275787/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-275787/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275787/field-3/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "047b7868-3069-5421-8c42-88cbce8eecae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275787/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "1694a284-2e0c-57d5-be06-d1408ca50c74" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275787/field-3/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-275787/field-3/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275787" :question/id #uuid "a39e36b1-acfe-5c9b-80de-88271f2bea5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275787" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+z=4x+y+2 \\\\ x+y=2z+2 \\\\ y=x-y+z+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $x=[x,y,z]^{T}$ of the system by computing the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x-y+z=2 \\\\ x+y-2z=2 \\\\ -x+2y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(-1+4)+(-1-2)+(2+1) \\\\  & =-9-3+3 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275787/field-1" "q-275787/field-2" "q-275787/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275787"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10100/selection/991e4a824b43068afb26935716245afeffa58d0034c9393d3cc698013ed59e01" :answer/id #uuid "28d683ca-b78e-5884-8031-7aa344c02867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-25,y=-12,z=100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10100/selection/9b0e6e8114bc44b7f020088046cf70cd883a1843fad771153b73d958db57a3f3" :answer/id #uuid "85720591-c3c6-53e8-901b-8a46af450252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-29,y=-12,z=-100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10100/selection/645a70af74f97752933896cec5290357fb6ac189250337dedbc0d81ec42ef774" :answer/id #uuid "36404c7a-d891-5302-8be7-5c5358b59cb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-29,y=-12,z=100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10100/selection/31e1a0642d790f594c6df1a0dff991155b541999c7ccbe40d76a7a0a390772b0" :answer/id #uuid "4b62fbb1-40ca-5d30-a9b4-4d10d82ad37d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=29,y=12,z=100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10100/selection/156458f548eb0832ae8363cc69936dbdbc2311628ee927ac559105e385cbc7b9" :answer/id #uuid "d0c8694e-1f8a-553f-b482-145cc731c605" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-29,y=-15,z=100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10100/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9cb38fb2-a8e7-502c-97f5-1c5f4b44e3d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10100/selection/645a70af74f97752933896cec5290357fb6ac189250337dedbc0d81ec42ef774" :answer-field/choices ["q-10100/selection/991e4a824b43068afb26935716245afeffa58d0034c9393d3cc698013ed59e01" "q-10100/selection/9b0e6e8114bc44b7f020088046cf70cd883a1843fad771153b73d958db57a3f3" "q-10100/selection/645a70af74f97752933896cec5290357fb6ac189250337dedbc0d81ec42ef774" "q-10100/selection/31e1a0642d790f594c6df1a0dff991155b541999c7ccbe40d76a7a0a390772b0" "q-10100/selection/156458f548eb0832ae8363cc69936dbdbc2311628ee927ac559105e385cbc7b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10100" :question/id #uuid "bb7ac4dc-2ca0-53a2-b162-9c25db67a37e" :question/math-academy-id "q-10100" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z=6 \\\\ 4x+7y+2z=0 \\\\ 3x+y+z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(7-2)-3(-2)+1(4-21) \\\\  & =10+6-17 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & -17 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -17 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -17 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -17 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 17 & -7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 17 & -7 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-29 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 100\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-29,y=-12,z=100.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10100/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10100"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78559/selection/0b32c2124c28a71c44090fa53c224a2ee89578c5ab0d826c3102ce47f805c882" :answer/id #uuid "ecaa0292-216a-5dc6-a0d9-a3bba9d13936" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and ${I}_{n}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78559/selection/d6df9cb1cc385fa6dc05c03afcc8f3c8668d726c8a7e671649deacba5b369b39" :answer/id #uuid "ca2b6089-557b-505d-a20e-aa0a59e23208" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D$ and $z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78559/selection/a090b3c4ebb689637d6f1266a496127112402301b2d02521ef96311abbfeb631" :answer/id #uuid "5dcb8e78-0495-5035-999d-fd53e3915d8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D$ and ${I}_{n}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78559/selection/a3e820060bdec1354ef2fd789004618e08cad206dceca229f3e1d5c848c2a2c2" :answer/id #uuid "d9f60717-b504-5ed2-adb6-facc3c8f2146" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $D$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78559/selection/b640c6d25e908183b2d950a6119ca0ce546d1f38b9d60a874fa13fcef4cd0bb2" :answer/id #uuid "6dcf2238-9cbe-58f7-9075-8cb15d057567" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and ${D}^{-1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78559/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9372ac19-df63-520d-897e-46af9d77d3c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78559/selection/0b32c2124c28a71c44090fa53c224a2ee89578c5ab0d826c3102ce47f805c882" :answer-field/choices ["q-78559/selection/0b32c2124c28a71c44090fa53c224a2ee89578c5ab0d826c3102ce47f805c882" "q-78559/selection/d6df9cb1cc385fa6dc05c03afcc8f3c8668d726c8a7e671649deacba5b369b39" "q-78559/selection/a090b3c4ebb689637d6f1266a496127112402301b2d02521ef96311abbfeb631" "q-78559/selection/a3e820060bdec1354ef2fd789004618e08cad206dceca229f3e1d5c848c2a2c2" "q-78559/selection/b640c6d25e908183b2d950a6119ca0ce546d1f38b9d60a874fa13fcef4cd0bb2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78559" :question/id #uuid "863bd08e-01cd-5a69-b3ce-bacc176f8b4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-78559" :question/problem "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,z=c.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $z$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $c$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,z & =c \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,z & =c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and right to left, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :question/worked-solution "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,z=c$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,z & =c \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,z & ={D}^{-1}c \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and ${I}_{n}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-78559/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-78442"] :question/problem "Consider a system of $3$ linear equations in $3$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,y=w.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $y$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $w$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w \\\\  & ={D}^{-1}\\,w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and left to right, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :question/worked-solution "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,y=w$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,y & ={D}^{-1}w \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w \\\\ y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and $y.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-78561/selection/a090b3c4ebb689637d6f1266a496127112402301b2d02521ef96311abbfeb631" :answer/id #uuid "be38daad-9f0f-52d8-99b5-268b10c565c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D$ and ${I}_{n}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78561/selection/3a54c4c53a882aa8fdb21b08af1a3c0a2fe983bfef1170f4ca828cd577740bc5" :answer/id #uuid "c9aeeb5d-fde3-5d0e-8807-a207ea073ef0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $t$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78561/selection/170eedf6c45e2a294f2e7256606688f50eac09f23de477fba074b8b707919c69" :answer/id #uuid "a518b603-68cf-5081-a006-bebec39c0ca9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $q$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78561/selection/a3e820060bdec1354ef2fd789004618e08cad206dceca229f3e1d5c848c2a2c2" :answer/id #uuid "d679bd28-9dfc-59b9-80cd-cc4e4da62788" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $D$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78561/selection/c598c956c752499ecebb196c84fec8c5b96e9412167062ae196e10ce787e80e7" :answer/id #uuid "3ff1d0cd-155c-5e4a-bb8b-1696cfc9d17a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D$ and $q$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78561/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "509dc752-679a-5a25-b0a5-555c3f377233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78561/selection/170eedf6c45e2a294f2e7256606688f50eac09f23de477fba074b8b707919c69" :answer-field/choices ["q-78561/selection/a090b3c4ebb689637d6f1266a496127112402301b2d02521ef96311abbfeb631" "q-78561/selection/3a54c4c53a882aa8fdb21b08af1a3c0a2fe983bfef1170f4ca828cd577740bc5" "q-78561/selection/170eedf6c45e2a294f2e7256606688f50eac09f23de477fba074b8b707919c69" "q-78561/selection/a3e820060bdec1354ef2fd789004618e08cad206dceca229f3e1d5c848c2a2c2" "q-78561/selection/c598c956c752499ecebb196c84fec8c5b96e9412167062ae196e10ce787e80e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78561" :question/id #uuid "ecf8e0a5-c1dd-5243-9116-de59a516e7ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-78561" :question/problem "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,t=q.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $t$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $q$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,t & =q \\\\ D\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\, \\\\ t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and left to right, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :question/worked-solution "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,t=q$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,t & =q \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and $q.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-78561/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78561"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78570/selection/710362311ddc3bc52513e1e2ddc794521971553b13e2205991db2c922f009345" :answer/id #uuid "6dca336a-9bd1-5f4c-b105-c4a1fd9599ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=B\\,d\\,A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78570/selection/b1d03968802a438a45e3feff90688a1d2be61935102210fac0de5ae74c6e61e6" :answer/id #uuid "a5398443-d933-535a-8142-8dc85e656ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=B\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78570/selection/0d61b819d3b8b7f6bc9f5eeae7a111cba6f55e8815d68dff3572972d2513f95e" :answer/id #uuid "406f002f-fb36-5105-b60e-69f49948948d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=AB\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78570/selection/63875f462eaa5a4f7c7dd738a0fe159658214a3db787653ac9c6f2b17eb1d8c0" :answer/id #uuid "f59f6906-172e-5218-a252-d5ab21e8ebdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}B\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78570/selection/228383024b3593d05de37eed2bb562e0d6a730857df66d9c3955eedff4ae2960" :answer/id #uuid "6da29be0-3677-5057-bf1e-921335a59b96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=BA\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78570/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6648f83-8783-5306-83de-7e3329a57e70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78570/selection/0d61b819d3b8b7f6bc9f5eeae7a111cba6f55e8815d68dff3572972d2513f95e" :answer-field/choices ["q-78570/selection/710362311ddc3bc52513e1e2ddc794521971553b13e2205991db2c922f009345" "q-78570/selection/b1d03968802a438a45e3feff90688a1d2be61935102210fac0de5ae74c6e61e6" "q-78570/selection/0d61b819d3b8b7f6bc9f5eeae7a111cba6f55e8815d68dff3572972d2513f95e" "q-78570/selection/63875f462eaa5a4f7c7dd738a0fe159658214a3db787653ac9c6f2b17eb1d8c0" "q-78570/selection/228383024b3593d05de37eed2bb562e0d6a730857df66d9c3955eedff4ae2960"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78570" :question/id #uuid "391ab7e6-9bff-528d-b143-5969ec37b9b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-78570" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x=B\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $7\\times 7$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $7\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x=B\\,d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}\\,x & =B\\,d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}\\,x & =AB\\,d \\\\ {I}_{7}\\,x & =AB\\,d \\\\ x & =AB\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78571/selection/598f110dac5f04047817583d8a729a776ea56d91c89f193fc2c23bbc26292422" :answer/id #uuid "0b6eff45-2b53-5342-b6be-ad7f718df3f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=A{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78571/selection/bae2a82734d751af89897db18b0455820aece6c2275be3d10ee697c5e7869a83" :answer/id #uuid "f8bd2c5c-914a-5ff4-9132-4f885d7db5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78571/selection/b7bfbfde50a91504394d1b413b591751c8a29ea1eefe3d2e7de9f4612e42e3a8" :answer/id #uuid "0db913f7-47b3-5c1e-8133-1d15c0b640c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78571/selection/c822a3635f9151eae99cc4f85624072a4ea0b574600ddb4dd37b274d1a11435c" :answer/id #uuid "e9410667-0a4e-5a73-9c2a-9fc6881ff150" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78571/selection/1a2b41fd4b275b0fd2bcf93816f3b806024cd77ac50caba5cac0c6f02de02f8b" :answer/id #uuid "159ea08a-8ea8-5765-b005-b2a6ddd80e2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78571/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc88e52-3b62-5dd4-929b-309a88df9ce1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78571/selection/bae2a82734d751af89897db18b0455820aece6c2275be3d10ee697c5e7869a83" :answer-field/choices ["q-78571/selection/598f110dac5f04047817583d8a729a776ea56d91c89f193fc2c23bbc26292422" "q-78571/selection/bae2a82734d751af89897db18b0455820aece6c2275be3d10ee697c5e7869a83" "q-78571/selection/b7bfbfde50a91504394d1b413b591751c8a29ea1eefe3d2e7de9f4612e42e3a8" "q-78571/selection/c822a3635f9151eae99cc4f85624072a4ea0b574600ddb4dd37b274d1a11435c" "q-78571/selection/1a2b41fd4b275b0fd2bcf93816f3b806024cd77ac50caba5cac0c6f02de02f8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78571" :question/id #uuid "e6242987-b8d2-5395-bc4d-b5736a798e19" :question/math-academy-id "q-78571" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $A\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times 2$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\,x & ={B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {A}^{-1}A\\,x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{2}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78571/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78571"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4520"] :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=3, y=0, z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=3+0+(-2)=1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4521"] :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3y+x+z=0 \\\\ z+4y-5=2 \\\\ 1+2x-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4604"] :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $B\\,\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\,\\mathbf{d},$ where $A$ and $B$ are $10 \\times 10$ non-singular matrices, while $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{d}$ are $10 \\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $\\mathbf{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse $B^{−1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\,\\mathbf{d}$ by $B^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{10}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
